@startuml
title Frontend location search with preview / commit
autonumber

actor Operator
participant "LocationSearch" as Search
participant "locationSearchRanking" as Rank
participant "NavigationWorkflow" as Nav
participant "MapController" as Map
participant "Breadcrumbs" as Crumbs

note over Search, Nav
  The "index" is the in-memory option list built once by
  NavigationWorkflow.getSearchOptions() from AdminTree.allNodes()
  (label = shapeName, path = "Country / Region / ...").
end note

Operator -> Search : click "Search location"
Search -> Search : expand panel, focus input
Operator -> Search : type query
Search -> Rank : rankLocationOptions(options, query)
note right of Rank
  No debounce: runs on every input event.
  < 2 chars -> nothing. Score: exact label 100,
  prefix 80, contains 60, path contains 30.
  Top 12, ties by path.
end note
Rank --> Search : ordered options
Search --> Operator : list of full paths

== Preview (hover or arrow keys) ==
Operator -> Search : pointer rests on / arrow to an option
Search -> Search : start 350 ms dwell timer
Search -> Nav : onPreviewStart(node) -> previewNode(node)
Nav -> Nav : capture snapshot once\n(selected, path, active, context, center, zoom)
Nav -> Nav : selectNode(node): update layers + navigation
Nav -> Map : fitViewToFeature or fitViewToFeatureHop
Nav -> Crumbs : setPath(path)

Operator -> Search : pointer leaves the list
Search -> Nav : onPreviewEnd() -> restorePreview()
Nav -> Nav : restore snapshot (layers, path, navigation)
Nav -> Map : hopToView(snapshot.center, snapshot.zoom)
Nav -> Crumbs : setPath(snapshot.path)

== Commit ==
Operator -> Search : click option or press Enter
alt option is the one being previewed
  Search -> Nav : onPreviewCommit(node) -> commitPreview(node)
  Nav -> Nav : drop snapshot, navigation.selected = node
else not previewing it
  Search -> Nav : endPreview, then onSelect(node) -> selectNode(node)
  Nav -> Map : select, choose transition, fit view
end
Search -> Search : collapse panel, clear input

note over Search
  Escape collapses the panel and ends any preview.
  Transition rule (navigationTransition): plain fit when going
  to the root or between ancestor/descendant; otherwise a "hop".
end note
@enduml
